package garden.xeno.symbolum.theories

/**
 * The command that writes `docs/lemmas.md`, which the document said it had and did not.
 *
 * The document has said of itself since it was written that it is *"generated from the code by
 * `Library.listing` and pinned by `LibrarySpec`"*. The second half was true and worked: the day the
 * library went from 76 entries to 106 the test went red and named the thirty that were missing. The
 * first half had no command behind it, and the file was last regenerated by adding a temporary test
 * that wrote the listing to a path taken from an environment variable, running it, and deleting it.
 * That works once and is not a procedure.
 *
 * It matters more than it looks, because of **when** the document breaks. It breaks exactly when
 * somebody adds a lemma, which is the moment they have least appetite for finding out how the file
 * is produced. The predictable outcome is a hand-pasted line, and from there the document stops
 * being generated and becomes a copy that resembles the output.
 *
 * == What it replaces, and what it leaves alone ==
 *
 * Only what lies between the two markers below. The prose above them — the excerpt, the argument
 * for why the file exists, the note about the three shared names — is written by hand and is worth
 * more than the listing; a generator that emitted the whole file would either lose it or would have
 * to carry it as a string literal, which is the same prose in a worse place.
 *
 * A file with no markers, or with them out of order, is refused by name rather than overwritten.
 * This writes over somebody's document and the one thing it must not do is guess where.
 */
object Lemmas {

  /** Where the listing goes, relative to the repository root. */
  val Document: String = "docs/lemmas.md"

  /** The command that runs this, written here so that the marker and the message cannot drift. */
  val Command: String = "sbt \"theories/runMain garden.xeno.symbolum.theories.Lemmas\""

  /**
   * The one generated region of the document, and the markers that delimit it.
   *
   * The mechanism moved to [[Generated]] on 2026-09-12 when `docs/proving.md` and
   * `docs/evaluation.md` gained generated tables of their own. Nothing about this document changed
   * except the markers, which now name their section: a document with three generated regions
   * cannot use an anonymous one, and two spellings of the same marker in one repository is the
   * second implementation this file's own note argues against.
   */
  val Section: Generated = Generated("lemmas", Document, Command)

  /** The line above the generated listing, in the document. */
  val Start: String = Section.start

  /** The line below it. */
  val End: String = Section.end

  /** The listing as the document carries it, which is every lemma the standard chain holds. */
  def listing(): String = {
    val chain = Chain.standard
    Library.of(chain).listing(chain.widest)
  }

  /** The document with its generated part replaced, or why it could not be. */
  def spliced(document: String, generated: String): Either[String, String] =
    Section.spliced(document, generated)

  /** What the generated part of a document currently holds, for a caller comparing the two. */
  def generatedPartOf(document: String): Either[String, String] = Section.partOf(document)

  def main(arguments: Array[String]): Unit =
    Generated.run(arguments, Document, Vector(Section -> listing()))
}
